From 69fcd94bad0a025916fdea8acff5ad0b28cc1d17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:19:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] PS1-FLAT: no 3D model in the house, the player is a
 billboard like every actor

Owner decision HOUSE CHARACTERS FLAT (2026-11-12): inside any house nobody
is drawn as a 3D model. ps1/src/room.c drew the player as model.c's chibi;
it now goes through the same billboard() as every resident, visitor, guest
and demon (the body sprite the core hands over: direction, walk frame, sit
squash; the same ordering slot and day light). The player keeps its contact
shadow, drawn as a billboard's.

The resting player stays: while its picture, place and squash have not
changed for two frames it is part of the backdrop and is drawn again only
inside the clips of what moves over it (without it the Hell-Cellar layout
runs at 18 fps instead of 28: everything in front of a moving element at
the back is drawn again every frame). A translucent player never rests.

Gone with the house's call: model.c g_model_hold, the per-polygon drawing
area g_r3_area (r3d.c, prims.c), room.c's player(), player_box(), ang_of().

home.txt (PCSX-Redux): plain 30.17 -> 30.17, steady 29.39 -> 30.00, orbit
27.27 -> 30.00, cellar_full 27.80 -> 27.80, defend_stress 19.25 -> 23.00,
modal 29.19 -> 30.00, defend_w3 30.13 -> 30.13, visit 30.17 -> 30.17; parity
pairs 0 px. Home group 130,856 -> 129,420 B; 496 B of resident code and
.bss freed. Core, GBA and Dreamcast files are untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
