From f00ed94f1f710aab05a1d2f618ebc3dc49f5b225 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:19:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] PS1-FLAT: model.c leaves resident RAM for the combat
 overlay group (+4,032 B)

With the house no longer calling it, the third-person chibi (model.c,
4,132 B of code) is needed only by plat_view3d's third-person views, which
only combat draws. ovl_plan.py: PLAT_GROUPS puts a platform file into a
group; GUARDED names the resident call that reaches it (view3d.c ->
model_player_draw), which is not followed. view3d.c asks
ovl_code_in(OVL_CODE_MODEL) (overlay.c) before the call and draws the
player's billboard if the combat group were ever not in the slot. The plan
fails when anything else would call the model (resident code, another
group such as the house, or an address that escapes).

prims.c (4,044 B) stays resident: with it the combat group would pass the
slot's size and the slot grows in 2 KB steps.

Game disc with the boot FMV: 65,952 -> 70,480 B below the stack top with the
commit before (+4,528 B in all); combat group 124,056 -> 128,188 B, slot
unchanged (131,072 B, set by the story group).

ps1/tools/test_ovl_guard.py (6 tests on a made-up game, in CI's PS1 job).
Third person exactly as before: perf_combat's 4 shots byte-identical,
fast_cellar_tp with the entropy pinned 183 of 184 shots byte-identical (one
frame differs by the adaptive view distance, which follows frame time), fps
28.86 -> 28.94; perf_combat 29.81 / 30.00 / 29.94 / 29.45 -> 29.88 / 30.00 /
29.94 / 29.51.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
